course: dictionary
lesson: 12599
title: Secrets Come Out: Disclosed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Disclosed is the past form of the verb disclose. It means told or made known something that was secret or private. «The shop disclosed the new prices on its website.» Before that day, nobody outside the shop knew the prices.
explain: You can also say «The price was not disclosed», which means nobody told the price. Undisclosed works the same way. «The team's new home is an undisclosed location» means the place is a secret.
explain: Disclosed can also mean uncovered or shown, when something hidden comes into view. «The fog lifted and disclosed a hidden valley.» The valley was there all along, but the fog had hidden it until it lifted.
fact: Disclosed is the past form of the verb disclose.
fact: «Disclosed» means told or made known, especially something that was secret or private.
fact: «Undisclosed» means not told or kept secret, as in «an undisclosed location».
fact: News reports often use disclosed: «The council disclosed the results of the survey.»
fact: A good check is to ask: was something secret, and now people know it? If yes, disclosed probably fits.
exercise: «The shop disclosed the new prices on its website.» What does disclosed mean? | Thrown away | Hidden under a rug | *Made known to everyone | Kept secret
exercise: «The team's new home is an undisclosed location.» What does undisclosed mean? | Clean and tidy | Known by everyone | Very loud | *Kept secret, not told
exercise: «When the workers dug the field, the spade disclosed an old coin.» Which word means the same as disclosed here? | lost | washed | *revealed | buried
test: «The company disclosed its profits in a report.» Disclosed here means | *Made public | Hid | Painted | Lost
test: Ruby says «The price was not disclosed». What does she mean? | The price was shown on every sign | *Nobody told the price | The price was made up by a clerk | The price was very high
exam: Which sentence uses disclosed to mean something hidden was revealed? | Mum bought a new coat | *The fog lifted and disclosed a hidden valley below | The cat hid under the bed | The bell rang at noon
